{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:97586","published":"2026-11-13T06:05:11.003704Z","modified":"2026-11-13T06:30:06.597594562Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-3592","CVE-2026-5950"],"summary":"Moderate: bind security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The Berkeley Internet Name Domain (BIND) is an implementation of the Domain Name System (DNS) protocols. BIND includes a DNS server (named); a resolver library (routines for applications to use when interfacing with DNS); and tools for verifying that the DNS server is operating correctly.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* bind: Amplification vulnerabilities via self-pointed glue records (CVE-2026-3592)\n\n* bind: Unbounded resend loop in BIND 9 resolver (CVE-2026-5950)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Bind 9.16.23 DNSSEC Key Rollover with KASP Causes ZSK Key To Be Removed Prematurely (JIRA:Rocky Linux-12487)\n\n* nslookup does not return and hang at epoll_wait() on some special occasions. (JIRA:Rocky Linux-29712)\n\n* Update to latest minor version 9.16.50 [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-6454)\n\n* pkcs11-tools test failing on engine (JIRA:Rocky Linux-213788)\n\n* dig on s390x does not return output when fails (JIRA:Rocky Linux-212648)\n\n* bind: New root trust anchor key for DNSSEC [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-255745)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nAdditional Changes:\n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the Rocky Linux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bind","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/bind?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:9.16.50-11.el9_9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"AppStream"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:97586